      "Version": "2026-10-05.1",
      "Sample": "contact_redline.tests.ps1#block-buyer-contact",
      "Status": "wired"
    },
    {
      "RuleId": "R-CONTACT-ROLE-ALLOWED",
      "Stage": "compliance",
      "Consumer": "Test-ContactRedline",
      "ConsumerFile": "scripts/lib/contact_rules.ps1",
      "Codes": [
        "CONTACT_ROLE_UNCLEAR",
        "CONTACT_ASK_UNAUTHORIZED_FIELD"
      ],
      "Evidence": "explicit consignee/recipient or supplier role + shipping/verification purpose, or this turn's AskFields authorization for THAT field key; a role that is authorized for one field does not authorize another (name != contact channel, supplier address != supplier contact)",
      "Version": "2026-10-05.3",
      "Sample": "third_fix_contact_fields.tests.ps1#C09",
      "Status": "wired"
    },
    {
      "RuleId": "R-REQUEST-ITEMS",
      "Stage": "compliance",
      "Consumer": "Get-ReplyRequestItems",
      "ConsumerFile": "scripts/lib/contact_rules.ps1",
      "Codes": [],
      "Evidence": "one structured request-item list (source span, action, verb source/inheritance, role, concrete FieldKey, purpose, collect/clarify) shared by Test-ContactRedline and Test-AskFieldConformance; a conjoined request inherits the ACTION but not the ROLE (purpose clauses, new verbs/owners, personal pronouns and sentence boundaries end the role scope)",
      "Version": "2026-10-05.3",
      "Sample": "third_fix_contact_fields.tests.ps1#C01",
      "Status": "wired"
    },
    {
      "RuleId": "R-CLARIFY-CANDIDATE-EVIDENCE",
      "Stage": "compliance",
      "Consumer": "Get-ReplyClarificationRequests",
      "ConsumerFile": "scripts/lib/reply_policy.ps1",
      "Codes": [
        "CLARIFY_CANDIDATE_UNSUPPORTED"
      ],
      "Evidence": "structured ClarificationRequests derived from the ONE fact model (CargoFacts.ByKey status + Conflicts.Candidates with value/unit/scope/source refs + Destination ambiguity). Every number in a clarification clause must match a real candidate (unit/scope consistent; only evidence-backed conversions are normalized); a bare ClarifyFields index or a scenario name never authorizes arbitrary values",
      "Version": "2026-10-05.3",
      "Sample": "third_fix_clarify.tests.ps1#Q01",
      "Status": "wired"
    },
    {
      "RuleId": "R-CONTACT-ASK-NO-ROLE",
      "Stage": "compliance",
      "Consumer": "Test-ContactRedline",
      "ConsumerFile": "scripts/lib/contact_rules.ps1",
      "Codes": [
        "CONTACT_ASK_NO_ROLE"
      ],
      "Evidence": "a contact request with no consignee/supplier business role; a shipping purpose such as 'for delivery updates' does not substitute for the role",
      "Version": "2026-10-05.2",
      "Sample": "review_fixes.tests.ps1#A1-generic-ask",
      "Status": "wired"
    },
    {
      "RuleId": "R-CONTACT-ASK-ALREADY-PROVIDED",
      "Stage": "compliance",
      "Consumer": "Test-ContactRedline",
      "ConsumerFile": "scripts/lib/contact_rules.ps1",
      "Codes": [
        "CONTACT_ASK_ALREADY_PROVIDED"
      ],
      "Evidence": "the concrete field key is already in this turn's facts (HasSupplierContact, or CargoFacts.ByKey supplier_contact / recipient_contact / recipient_name / supplier_address / delivery_address = provided) - asking again is blocked, and an AskFields authorization never overrides an already-provided field (recipient_name does not prove recipient_contact)",
      "Version": "2026-10-05.3",
      "Sample": "third_fix_contact_fields.tests.ps1#C08",
      "Status": "wired"
    },
    {
      "RuleId": "R-CONTACT-MIXED-CLAUSE",
      "Stage": "compliance",
      "Consumer": "Get-ContactClauses",
      "ConsumerFile": "scripts/lib/contact_rules.ps1",
